WEBVTT

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.320
Abeno-dono, sorry for all the trouble.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:05.080
Not at all.

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:06.400
Haruitsuki!

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:06.980
Huh?

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:11.440
My head still stings where 
Ashiya hit me with his shoe.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:12.490
Let it go.

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:14.960
He couldn't see you.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.370
What? He can't see?

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.370
Has Ashiya-dono's vision

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:25.180
not returned since he gave it to Tomori?

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:29.630
Tomori said it would return in two 
or three days. Surely she wasn't...

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:32.140
Don't trouble yourself.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:35.010
Tomori-dono wasn't lying.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:38.960
You went all the way to the Underworld 
to ask Tomori about it, right?

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:41.760
It wasn't like that.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:43.960
I just asked her since I was already there.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:46.060
What did Tomori say?

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:50.120
The time it takes for someone's vision

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:52.530
to return varies from person to person.

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:54.880
But if it's taking a while,

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:57.770
there may be some other reason for it.

00:00:57.770 --> 00:00:58.760
I see.

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:00.880
Tomori-dono fears

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:04.000
that he may lose his vision 
forever if he remains unable

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.300
to see for too long.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:09.530
Do you know why this is happening?

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:13.140
It's just a guess, but I do have an idea.

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:15.700
I see. So that's why...

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:20.240
I did think it seemed awfully 
lively outside the shrine.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.560
I should go, Okina-dono. See you later.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:26.690
It would seem that it's nothing to worry about.

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:30.190
I hope you're right.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:32.330
Yahiko, I'm counting on you.

00:01:32.330 --> 00:01:33.940
Hey, Haruitsuki.

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:36.480
If you want me to help you 
with your job tomorrow,

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:37.920
give me more treats.

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:39.880
Sure. What do you want?

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:43.770
Rakugan and dumplings and 
steamed buns and potato chips...

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.500
And, uh...

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:20.470
<b>Mystery 13 "The End"</b>

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:19.230
In this case, the problem can 
be solved using this formula.

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:20.810
First we substitute for x...

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:22.270
<i>He's out again today.</i>

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:23.210
Ashiya.

00:03:23.210 --> 00:03:24.700
<i>Of course I'm worried.</i>

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:26.200
Hey, Ashiya!

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:26.970
Y-Yes?

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:29.370
What are you spacing out for?

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:31.360
S-Sorry.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:33.910
If you feel sick, do you want 
to go to the nurse's office?

00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:35.950
No, I'm fine.

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:38.810
Is this the return of 
Hanae-chan of the Nurse's Office?

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:41.990
Okay, quiet. Let's continue.

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:48.120
We're going to the convenience store 
since our club's off today.

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:49.950
Ashiyan, what are you going to do?

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:50.800
I'll go.

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:52.360
I'm getting a croquette today.

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:55.250
Yesterday's croquette sure was good.

00:03:57.780 --> 00:03:59.020
Clean well.

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:00.040
Hanae...

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:02.880
Do you have a minute?

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:07.020
Sorry. You guys go on ahead.

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:09.640
Yahiko?

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:13.720
He's been gone since yesterday morning,
when he said he was going

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:15.640
to help Abeno with his work.

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:17.950
Is he helping in my place?

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:21.000
Who knows? He tends to disappear

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.630
for two or three days at a time.

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:25.740
I hope Fuzzy's okay.

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:29.100
He's still afraid of Yahiko.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:30.840
I hope they're getting along.

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:32.040
Anyway,

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:35.040
it won't do any good for me to worry about it.

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:37.550
What?

00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:41.110
Nothing. You still can't see, huh?

00:04:42.070 --> 00:04:45.750
Since it's been this long and I still can't, maybe...

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:47.600
it's time I gave up.

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:48.840
I just remembered.

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:53.430
I think Yahiko mentioned something 
about a mountain shrine.

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:54.700
A shrine?

00:04:56.070 --> 00:04:57.300
<i>Could it be...</i>

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:04.310
<i>There's no point in worrying 
about it, now that I can't see.</i>

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:07.640
<i>I should forget. I should forget, and...</i>

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.580
<b>No Unauthorized Entry</b>

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:11.580
Huh?

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:19.530
Why did I come here?

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:32.350
<i>I can try to forget all I want.</i>

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:36.850
<i>But there's no way I can</i>

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:41.740
<i>forget right away.</i>

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:47.610
I can't focus.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:55.270
<i>I hope Jomatsu-san and the 
princess are getting along.</i>

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:57.140
Huh?

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:02.340
Must've been my imagination.

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:05.040
<i>I still have my habits from work.</i>

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:06.970
<i>I'm weirdly sensitive to my surroundings.</i>

00:06:07.230 --> 00:06:09.610
Okay, time to study.

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:14.520
<i>If Abeno-san took Yahiko with him,</i>

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:17.030
<i>it must be a difficult job.</i>

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:20.700
It's no use! I can't stop thinking about it!

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:23.240
In fact, I'm even more worried 
now than I was before!

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:37.990
Did something just fly past me?

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:47.720
What was that? Was I just laughing out loud?

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:49.660
It was like...

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:54.390
Could it be that I've lost not just 
my sight, but my mind, too?

00:06:55.940 --> 00:06:57.340
This is it.

00:06:57.340 --> 00:06:59.520
I came all the way here, but now...

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:02.010
<i>What am I doing?</i>

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:05.240
<i>Coming here won't change anything.</i>

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:08.710
Abeno-san! Yahiko!

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:10.780
I guess I wouldn't know if he were here.

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:13.830
Abeno-san! Hey!

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:18.230
I thought something might 
have happened to them,

00:07:18.690 --> 00:07:21.170
but I guess I was overthinking it.

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:23.610
That's just as well, though.

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:28.600
I'll look around the area before going home.

00:07:38.610 --> 00:07:41.070
What is this?! A y-yokai?!

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:43.810
Does this mean my vision is back? 
Am I back to normal?!

00:07:46.470 --> 00:07:48.820
<i>Is this butterbur leaf...</i>

00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:51.480
Okina-sama?

00:07:52.940 --> 00:07:54.200
Wait!

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:57.450
Did Abeno-san and a fox yokai come here?

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:00.200
They're inside?

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:04.210
Abeno-san?

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:06.220
Is anyone here?

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:09.130
There's no one here.

00:08:10.070 --> 00:08:11.220
Okina-sama?

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:15.800
<i>That's...</i>

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:20.350
I was right.

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:22.230
It's the Mononokean's crest.

00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:24.900
H-Huh?

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:30.780
I got dirt in my eye.

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:43.000
<b>The Morose Mononokean</b>

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:47.000
Um...

00:08:47.430 --> 00:08:50.380
O-Okina-sama?

00:08:51.320 --> 00:08:53.770
Huh? It's not him?

00:08:53.770 --> 00:08:55.300
Oh, okay...

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:58.520
B-But you're a yokai, right?

00:08:58.520 --> 00:09:01.070
I can't see yokai right now,

00:09:01.070 --> 00:09:04.170
so I can't tell what you look like...

00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:07.940
No, calm down. If he's a yokai, it's okay.

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:11.820
Did you invite me in here

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:13.690
so I could exorcise you?

00:09:15.890 --> 00:09:17.080
That's not it?

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:19.740
Um, then...

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:20.900
Why?

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:33.880
I'm surrounded?

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:37.160
What should I do?

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:38.890
I'm so scared.

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:41.890
<i>Of course I am.</i>

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:46.520
<i>I originally hated horror and creepy stuff.</i>

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:49.180
<i>I got used to it after I started 
working at the Mononokean,</i>

00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:52.400
<i>so I guess I stopped feeling 
cautious around yokai.</i>

00:09:52.750 --> 00:09:56.970
<i>And it's not as if Abeno-san 
is exorcising yokai for fun.</i>

00:09:56.970 --> 00:09:59.160
<i>If he kept someone who can't see around,</i>

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:01.530
<i>he'd never get anything done, 
so he drew the line.</i>

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:04.970
<i>But I didn't like how he said it,</i>

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:06.640
<i>so I lashed out at him.</i>

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:10.670
<i>And despite that, I was worried 
about him and came here...</i>

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:13.620
<i>And now I'm curled up in fear.</i>

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:15.660
<i>What am I doing?</i>

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:22.550
<i>I'm not sure if that thing is 
a yokai or something else...</i>

00:10:22.820 --> 00:10:26.780
<i>But it probably knows something about them.</i>

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:30.810
<i>Why am I being so useless at 
a critical time like this?</i>

00:10:34.290 --> 00:10:35.630
<i>I can't see them,</i>

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:40.700
<i>but I'm sure something is 
here, surrounding me...</i>

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:42.950
Huh? What is this?

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:45.930
<i>They're definitely looking at me.</i>

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:47.260
<i>I can sense it clearly.</i>

00:10:47.720 --> 00:10:51.460
<i>But this feeling isn't hostility or fear.</i>

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:53.930
No, I can't see them.

00:10:53.930 --> 00:10:56.340
How would I know that?

00:10:57.640 --> 00:11:00.590
But it's somehow

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:04.350
warm and kind.

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:22.320
Don't throw that away!

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:23.920
Where'd you get that skull?

00:11:23.920 --> 00:11:26.510
I found it in the mountains. Nice, isn't it?

00:11:26.510 --> 00:11:27.310
Go throw it out.

00:11:27.310 --> 00:11:28.620
What?!

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:31.000
He's fast asleep.

00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:33.880
He must be out cold.

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:36.880
Shouldn't we wake him now?

00:11:37.890 --> 00:11:40.630
What do you think, Princess Anmo?

00:11:41.910 --> 00:11:43.260
Again?!

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:45.110
Would you be willing

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:48.710
to do that for us?

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:03.910
Fuzzy...

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:05.220
Don't sleep.

00:12:07.480 --> 00:12:09.210
Huh... Huh?

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:11.530
Huh?!

00:12:11.530 --> 00:12:14.990
Big Boss Scree! Mitsuchigura-san! Manjirou!

00:12:14.990 --> 00:12:16.760
Spiny! Nobou-san!

00:12:16.760 --> 00:12:19.280
Jomatsu-san! Princess Anmo!

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:20.920
And... Abeno-san!

00:12:22.310 --> 00:12:26.560
He asked us to help restore your vision.

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:27.430
Mine?

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:30.200
Yes. If you're ever in trouble,

00:12:30.200 --> 00:12:33.310
your friends will always come 
running to help, Ashiya-dono.

00:12:33.760 --> 00:12:35.560
But how?

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:38.040
Don't get the wrong idea, kid.

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:41.260
I just tagged along since I was delivering

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:43.400
a gift to the Mononokean.

00:12:44.980 --> 00:12:47.280
You seem to be all better now.

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:53.200
I can see him!

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:54.570
I can see him clearly!

00:12:54.570 --> 00:12:57.080
My vision is back! It's Fuzzy!

00:12:57.080 --> 00:12:59.040
You just realized that?

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:01.550
Ah, that was fun!

00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:05.680
Ashiya, you were on the verge of tears.

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:06.850
Huh?

00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:09.210
Then that skull...

00:13:09.990 --> 00:13:11.430
You were teasing me, Yahiko?!

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:14.140
But because I scared you,

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:15.940
you're back to normal!

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:17.070
Huh?

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:19.600
I told him to give you a little scare.

00:13:19.600 --> 00:13:23.390
Abeno-san, what in the world is going on?

00:13:23.390 --> 00:13:26.270
Does it matter? You can see now.

00:13:26.270 --> 00:13:28.790
That's certainly good news...

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:32.300
But what are all these yokai doing here?

00:13:32.300 --> 00:13:35.580
How come I can see them now?

00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:37.500
Why? Why, Abeno-san?

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:39.340
Ugh, you're so annoying.

00:13:41.020 --> 00:13:45.080
Think about what first triggered 
your ability to see yokai.

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:46.220
The trigger?

00:13:46.690 --> 00:13:49.080
The first yokai I saw

00:13:49.080 --> 00:13:50.920
was Fuzzy lying on the ground.

00:13:50.920 --> 00:13:53.470
What were you thinking about then?

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:55.520
I don't remember.

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:59.290
Probably what my high school 
life had in store for me.

00:13:59.290 --> 00:14:01.770
It was probably some stupid nonsense.

00:14:01.770 --> 00:14:03.610
That's not nonsense!

00:14:03.870 --> 00:14:08.240
That's why I thought the trigger 
wasn't you, but the hairball.

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:10.240
Fuzzy granted me my ability?

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:14.840
No, your predisposition reacted to him.

00:14:14.840 --> 00:14:16.750
To what he was feeling.

00:14:17.440 --> 00:14:19.620
To Fuzzy's feelings?

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:22.200
So I thought exposing you to the same situation

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:24.000
might restore your vision.

00:14:24.440 --> 00:14:25.510
After all,

00:14:26.680 --> 00:14:28.070
it seems these yokai

00:14:28.640 --> 00:14:31.740
hold special feelings for you.

00:14:31.740 --> 00:14:34.220
We were by your side,

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:37.520
praying for your vision to return.

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:40.320
What? So everything that happened...

00:14:40.320 --> 00:14:44.840
As expected, you and your 
peculiar devotion to yokai

00:14:44.840 --> 00:14:47.530
responded to them.

00:14:47.530 --> 00:14:51.220
Peculiar? Am I peculiar?

00:14:52.840 --> 00:14:55.400
I'm sorry for the inconvenience.

00:14:58.050 --> 00:14:59.660
You should thank them.

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:04.920
They came all the way from 
the Underworld for you.

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:07.420
Thank you so much.

00:15:08.690 --> 00:15:09.800
See you later.

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:12.830
Take care of yourself, kid.

00:15:12.830 --> 00:15:13.930
You, too, Manjirou.

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:16.670
Come see us in the Underworld.

00:15:18.280 --> 00:15:21.280
Our friendship is eternal.

00:15:21.280 --> 00:15:23.060
Thank you, Nobou-san.

00:15:23.320 --> 00:15:25.880
Mitsuchigura-san, thank you, too.

00:15:25.880 --> 00:15:29.820
I'm not the one you should be thanking.

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:30.800
Huh?

00:15:30.800 --> 00:15:34.000
Abeno-sama, if you would.

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:34.780
Sure.

00:15:47.760 --> 00:15:51.850
<i>I'm so glad to have exorcised them.</i>

00:15:52.320 --> 00:15:53.550
Come to think of it...

00:15:53.870 --> 00:15:54.870
Abeno-san!

00:15:55.550 --> 00:15:59.130
My vision seems to have leveled up!

00:15:59.130 --> 00:16:01.520
I can see ghosts now!

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:02.060
What?

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:04.680
A hand reached out from that wall

00:16:04.680 --> 00:16:06.920
and grabbed my clothes!

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:08.820
Oh, that was...

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:10.820
Okina-sama is calling you.

00:16:11.250 --> 00:16:12.820
Is it a new job?

00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:15.690
What is this?

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:19.200
Huh? Ashiya?

00:16:19.470 --> 00:16:20.640
And that's what happened.

00:16:20.640 --> 00:16:22.920
Your vision hadn't returned completely,

00:16:22.920 --> 00:16:24.960
so you just saw my hand, right?

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:26.960
That was the scariest part!

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:31.340
I called Abeno-dono because you 
seemed to be looking for him.

00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:34.400
Forgive me for scaring you.

00:16:34.400 --> 00:16:37.660
Why did you come here, anyway?

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:41.480
You haven't been to school all this time,

00:16:41.480 --> 00:16:43.230
so I was worried...

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:45.520
I know what you're going to say.

00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:48.360
I couldn't have done you 
any good by coming here.

00:16:48.620 --> 00:16:52.810
But I'm relieved your vision has returned.

00:16:52.810 --> 00:16:54.610
Right, Abeno-dono?

00:16:55.400 --> 00:16:56.220
I guess.

00:16:56.220 --> 00:16:58.120
It would've been terrible if it hadn't.

00:16:58.120 --> 00:17:01.390
You went all the way to the 
Underworld to bring them—

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:04.880
Go throw that skull away.

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:07.510
Haruitsuki, what was that for?

00:17:07.510 --> 00:17:08.750
Just go throw it out.

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:10.860
But I want to show Zenko, too.

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:12.860
You shouldn't carelessly 
bring skulls into temples.

00:17:12.860 --> 00:17:15.040
I'll put it back in the 
mountains once I show Zenko.

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:16.580
Huh? What?!

00:17:17.560 --> 00:17:18.510
Haruitsuki.

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:20.320
I see!

00:17:20.320 --> 00:17:24.560
Abeno-san, you called all 
those yokai here for me?

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:26.270
And you said I was fired!

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:28.540
Okina-dono...

00:17:29.930 --> 00:17:32.250
Abeno-san, I didn't know you were there,

00:17:32.250 --> 00:17:35.280
but I'm sorry for throwing my shoe at you.

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:37.030
You should be apologizing to me for that!

00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:38.320
To you?

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:41.050
You hit my forehead!

00:17:41.050 --> 00:17:42.750
What? You were on the roof?

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:44.200
I really am sorry!

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:46.250
I'll forgive you for ten dumplings.

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:47.880
Glazed? Red bean?

00:17:47.880 --> 00:17:48.900
Both!

00:17:49.990 --> 00:17:51.540
I'll get those.

00:17:51.540 --> 00:17:55.020
No, it's okay. I'll buy some at 
the convenience store tomorrow.

00:17:55.020 --> 00:17:55.830
Ashiya.

00:17:56.790 --> 00:17:57.770
Yes?

00:17:58.680 --> 00:18:01.810
I was rude to you yesterday.

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:07.310
Will you work for me again as 
an employee of the Mononokean,

00:18:07.680 --> 00:18:08.790
Ashiya-dono?

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:14.650
Don't bow your head to me!

00:18:14.650 --> 00:18:17.040
You're the one who told me to do it.

00:18:17.040 --> 00:18:17.630
So?

00:18:17.630 --> 00:18:19.110
So? So...

00:18:19.970 --> 00:18:20.570
Yes!

00:18:21.570 --> 00:18:25.330
I'll continue to do my very best,
so please accept my humble work!

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:27.030
<i>He's groveling...</i>

00:18:29.630 --> 00:18:31.450
That tickles.

00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:32.340
<i>Your best, huh?</i>

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:33.500
Hey, come on...

00:18:37.570 --> 00:18:40.300
<i>Your very best is terrifying indeed.</i>

00:18:43.990 --> 00:18:44.600
What?

00:18:44.880 --> 00:18:47.600
Fuzzy was with me the whole time?

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:49.600
Pulling him off of you seemed

00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:52.590
like it would make him grow 
infinitely huge out of anxiety.

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:55.720
Fuzzy, I'm sorry I didn't notice.

00:18:55.720 --> 00:18:57.430
How can I make it up to you?

00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:00.700
What?

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:05.700
Oh, fine.

00:19:03.440 --> 00:19:05.700
Don't joke around with speech bubbles.

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:10.210
I guess I'll play ball with you.

00:19:07.190 --> 00:19:10.210
"I guess I'll play ball with you"?

00:19:10.210 --> 00:19:12.960
I guess I'll play ball with you.

00:19:11.560 --> 00:19:12.960
That's no problem at all!

00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:17.380
I guess I'll play ball with you.

00:19:13.670 --> 00:19:15.400
Mononokean, thanks for translating.

00:19:15.400 --> 00:19:17.340
I had no idea you could do that.

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:18.970
I was just guessing.

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:26.430
I was just guessing.

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:21.320
Let's go, Fuzzy.

00:19:21.320 --> 00:19:23.160
You are both yokai.

00:19:23.720 --> 00:19:26.260
You may have been guessing, 
but it looks like you were right.

00:19:28.690 --> 00:19:30.600
Okay, here we go, Fuzzy!

00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:31.810
There!

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:34.310
Nice catch!

00:19:35.760 --> 00:19:39.750
Long ago, I couldn't reach this wind chime.

00:19:39.750 --> 00:19:41.850
But I was determined to touch it,

00:19:42.400 --> 00:19:44.950
so I had Aoi lift me up.

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:52.830
To me, it feels like that was only yesterday.

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:49.640
Does it make you uneasy that a 
human like me became the master,

00:19:49.640 --> 00:19:52.730
and I've even hired a human employee?

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:54.460
Aren't you the one who's uneasy?

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:01.210
For yokai, living with humans

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:11.310
Aren't you the one who's uneasy?

00:20:01.210 --> 00:20:04.400
depends on a set of very fragile conditions.

00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:07.640
Even if you can coexist, unlike yokai,

00:20:08.200 --> 00:20:11.180
there's a limit to how 
many years humans live.

00:20:11.350 --> 00:20:12.730
That's why we...

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:16.730
can never get close to humans.

00:20:18.730 --> 00:20:21.440
can never get close to humans.

00:20:19.220 --> 00:20:21.420
He'll realize that eventually.

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:31.960
So that's what you were worried about.

00:20:23.750 --> 00:20:26.760
Mononokean, what about you?

00:20:26.760 --> 00:20:29.500
Yokai employees could work here longer.

00:20:29.500 --> 00:20:31.640
If it makes you uneasy, I'll reconsider it.

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:33.750
I...

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:36.000
I...

00:20:36.040 --> 00:20:39.750
I obey the will of my master.

00:20:42.950 --> 00:20:43.940
I see.

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:46.020
But now,

00:20:46.280 --> 00:20:50.010
I'm sooo happy to have Hanae back!

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:56.600
I'm sooo happy to have Hanae back!

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:56.740
I see. But...

00:20:56.650 --> 00:21:03.900
What's wrong?

00:20:58.070 --> 00:21:00.880
We were able to use those yokai's feelings

00:21:00.880 --> 00:21:03.900
to restore Ashiya's vision this time.

00:21:04.220 --> 00:21:06.410
But it only took a single yokai,

00:21:04.490 --> 00:21:05.690
Here it comes again!

00:21:06.930 --> 00:21:08.910
the hairball, to awaken his abilities.

00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:13.220
So shouldn't the hairball's feelings 
have been enough to restore his sight?

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:16.170
He must have been waiting for him.

00:21:14.930 --> 00:21:16.030
Waiting?

00:21:16.210 --> 00:21:18.420
He believed Hanae wouldn't abandon him.

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:23.550
Wouldn't abandon him, huh?

00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:26.050
Come on, throw the ball back.

00:21:28.280 --> 00:21:29.430
Hey, Fuzzy.

00:21:32.020 --> 00:21:33.100
Thank you.

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:33.770
Huh?

00:21:48.950 --> 00:21:52.420
You're so darn cute!

00:21:54.770 --> 00:21:55.770
Abeno-san.

00:21:55.770 --> 00:21:56.480
Yeah?

00:21:56.480 --> 00:21:59.690
Would it be okay if Fuzzy 
stayed at my house tonight?

00:21:59.690 --> 00:22:00.580
What?!

00:22:01.670 --> 00:22:02.980
Oh, I guess so.
